-- facts/layering.rofl — THE DECLARATIONS FOR THE ENGINE/LIBRARY SPLIT.
--
-- The owner's, like `layer(L)` and `role_decl(R)`. An executor may not add a
-- library to make a crossing legal, and may not widen the surface to make an
-- audit go quiet.

-- ============================================================== THE SURFACE
-- WHAT A LIBRARY MAY ENTER THE ENGINE THROUGH. Two files, and the second is
-- there for the storage port rather than for a domain library.
--
-- MEASURED: 26 of the 28 imports the JS model makes into `src/` already go to
-- `src/api.ts`. The surface is small because the tree already treats it as
-- small, not because a rule was imposed.
surface_decl("src/api.ts").
surface_decl("src/store.ts").
-- AND `boot.rofl`, WHICH THE FIRST RUN GOT WRONG. It reported 29 deep
-- crossings and 26 of them were a library LOADING THE SEMANTICS — which is not
-- reaching into the engine's insides, it is the engine's front door in its
-- other form. A library that could not load boot.rofl could not use the
-- language at all. The tell was that the audit named one target 26 times: an
-- audit whose rows are mostly one destination is usually wrong about that
-- destination rather than right about the sources.
surface_decl("boot.rofl").

-- ============================================================= THE LIBRARIES
-- `library_decl(Name, PathPrefix)`. One library today; the whole point of the
-- decision is that there will be more, and a second one costs four facts.
library_decl(js, "rules/js-").
library_decl(js, "facts/js-").
library_decl(js, "scanners/js").
library_decl(js, "test/js-").
library_decl(js, "test/fixtures/js-").

-- ================================================================== RULINGS
-- `side_decl(Path, Side)` overrides location. Empty on the first pass: every
-- assignment below is currently by location, and a ruling here should be a
-- decision somebody made after reading the audit.
